Subject: [PATCH] SdSpiCard: retry failed transfers, then initialize the card again

FOs: on the reTerminal Sticky the SD card shares its SPI bus with the e-paper
panel, and its chip select does not isolate it, so the card sees display
traffic as commands. With USE_SD_CRC it rejects nearly all of them, but the
first transfer afterwards can still fail, and a stray reset leaves the card
idle until it is initialized again. Retry a failed sector transfer once, then
run begin() with the saved configuration and retry once more.

---
--- a/src/SdCard/SdSpiCard/SdSpiCard.h
+++ b/src/SdCard/SdSpiCard/SdSpiCard.h
@@ -288,6 +288,18 @@ class SdSpiCard {
   bool writeStop();
 
  private:
+  // Single attempts behind the retrying public transfers.
+  bool readSectorsOnce(Sector_t sector, uint8_t* dst, size_t ns);
+  bool writeSectorOnce(Sector_t sector, const uint8_t* src);
+  bool writeSectorsOnce(Sector_t sector, const uint8_t* src, size_t ns);
+  // Recover after two failed attempts by initializing the card again.
+  bool reinitAfterFailure();
+  // SdSpiConfig has const members, so keep its fields.
+  SdCsPin_t m_reinitCsPin = 0;
+  uint8_t m_reinitOptions = 0;
+  uint32_t m_reinitMaxSck = 0;
+  SpiPort_t* m_reinitPort = nullptr;
+  bool m_reinitValid = false;
   // private functions
   uint8_t cardAcmd(uint8_t cmd, uint32_t arg) {
     cardCommand(CMD55, 0);
